hundreds ran in panic as a powerful  storm hit the stage crushing into the  crowds with little warnings strong winds  toppled the rigging leaving people  desperate to escape steel scaffolding  and heavy beams collapsed onto the  terrified concert goers one witness  filmed a chaotic scenes and describes  the moment the stage came down curious  police I couldn't believe it I just  swung around to catch the tarps blowing  in the wind and then just disbelief as  they try to leave the stadium hundreds  lifted heavy beams and machinery to  rescue the injured many of whom were in  the VIP section closest to the stage you  see it happens and you just ask it did  it really happen I didn't know issues  that and then she pulled me out from  underneath and I couldn't find my best  friend and she found me and I found my  mom  strangers didn't care it was like  everybody knew everybody because they  were there for one effort and I was to  make sure everybody was getting the  treatment thing he didn't take care of  emergency services had been monitoring  the concert waiting for a storm but its  severity and timing was unexpected four  people were killed and many more injured  at least 40 people that were injured and  transported to area hospitals the degree  of injuries for those people ranges from  cuts and scrapes to very serious  injuries and I would be I want to be  very frank that there is a possibility  that we could have other deaths a  memorial service honoring the victims  will be held tomorrow  Lisa Casa Sky News
 

